'IIIT Pune Recruitment 2026: 25 Teaching and Non-Teaching Posts, Apply by 28 November 2026',
'',
'IIIT Pune has opened applications for 25 teaching and non-teaching posts, with online applications open from 29 October 2026 to 28 November 2026 and hard-copy applications due by 9 December 2026.',
'',
$$<p>The Indian Institute of Information Technology Pune has opened applications for 25 teaching and non-teaching posts, with online applications open from 29 October 2026 to 28 November 2026. The IIIT Pune recruitment 2026 covers 17 Assistant Professor posts and eight Group B non-teaching posts at the institute in Pune, Maharashtra. The recruitment is set out in two October 2026 notifications, and both windows close at 11.59 pm on 28 November 2026.</p>
<p>An online form alone does not complete this application. Candidates must also print the completed form, sign it, attach the payment receipt and self-attested supporting documents, and send the set to the Registrar so that it reaches the institute by 5.30 pm on 9 December 2026. The institute has clarified that eligibility will be assessed on the basis of the hard-copy application received within that deadline.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance: IIIT Pune recruitment 2026</th><th>Detail</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Indian Institute of Information Technology Pune</td></tr><tr><td>Total posts</td><td>25 (17 teaching, 8 non-teaching)</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Pune, Maharashtra</td></tr><tr><td>Apply from</td><td>29 October 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Online deadline</td><td>28 November 2026, 11.59 pm</td></tr><tr><td>Hard-copy deadline</td><td>9 December 2026, 5.30 pm</td></tr><tr><td>Teaching portal</td><td>iiitprec.samarth.edu.in</td></tr><tr><td>Non-teaching portal</td><td>iiitpnt.samarth.edu.in</td></tr></table>
<h2>IIIT Pune recruitment 2026 teaching posts</h2>
<p>The teaching recruitment covers 17 Assistant Professor posts across three departments: Computer Science and Engineering, Electronics and Communication Engineering, and Applied Science and Humanities. Six posts are Assistant Professor Grade I, at Pay Level 12, with three unreserved, one OBC, one SC and one EWS vacancy. Eleven posts are Assistant Professor Grade II, at Pay Level 10, with six unreserved, four OBC and one EWS vacancy, and these Grade II appointments are contractual. Candidates should check the detailed advertisement for the preferred specialisations in each department before choosing where to apply.</p>
<p>IIIT Pune is an Institute of National Importance, established in 2016 by the Ministry of Education with industry partners under a not-for-profit public-private partnership model. The institute said additional shortlisting criteria are based on research publications, institutional background and relevant experience, alongside the essential qualifications set out below.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the IIIT Pune teaching posts</h2>
<p>For both teaching grades, applicants must hold a PhD in the relevant or equivalent discipline, along with first-class performance in their preceding degrees. Where an institution does not define first class, at least 60 per cent marks or a 6.5 CGPA will be treated as first class. For Assistant Professor Grade II, the PhD is the prescribed essential qualification, with no minimum experience or credit-point requirement stated.</p>
<p>For Assistant Professor Grade I, candidates must hold a PhD and either three years of post-PhD experience or six years of total teaching and research experience in eligible institutions, research laboratories or relevant industries. They must also satisfy a requirement of 20 cumulative essential credit points. A separate application and fee are needed for each post and department applied for, and the teaching fee, including 18 per cent GST, is Rs. 2,360 per department per post for General, OBC and EWS candidates and Rs. 1,180 for SC, ST, female and PwBD candidates. Regular IIIT Pune employees are exempt from the fee.</p>
<h2>IIIT Pune non-teaching posts and eligibility</h2>
<p>The non-teaching recruitment covers eight Group B posts, all at Pay Level 6 under the Seventh Central Pay Commission: six Junior Superintendent posts, one Junior Engineer (Civil) post and one Junior Engineer (Electrical) post. For Junior Superintendent, applicants must hold a first-class bachelor's degree with six years of relevant experience, or a postgraduate qualification with four years of relevant experience. For the Junior Engineer posts, applicants must hold an engineering degree in the relevant discipline with two years of experience, or an engineering diploma with five years of relevant experience.</p>
<p>The upper age limit for the advertised non-teaching posts is 32 years, subject to applicable relaxations. The non-teaching fee is Rs. 1,180 for UR, OBC and EWS candidates and Rs. 885 for SC, ST, female and PwBD candidates, and regular IIIT Pune employees are again exempt. Candidates should confirm the reservation position in the detailed non-teaching notification before applying.</p>
<h2>IIIT Pune recruitment 2026 selection process</h2>
<p>For teaching posts, eligible candidates will be screened and shortlisted on the institute's criteria and departmental requirements. Shortlisted candidates will undergo document verification and an offline written test at the IIIT Pune campus. The written test is qualifying in nature, while final selection will depend on performance in the research and teaching presentation and interview that follow it.</p>
<p>For non-teaching posts, the selection process includes screening, a written examination and a job-oriented practical test, with the applicable assessment scheme varying by post. Applicants employed by government bodies, public sector undertakings or educational institutions should apply through the proper channel or provide the required No Objection Certificate and vigilance clearance certificate before the online deadline.</p>
<h2>How to apply for IIIT Pune recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>First, choose the correct portal: teaching applicants use iiitprec.samarth.edu.in and non-teaching applicants use iiitpnt.samarth.edu.in. Register on the relevant portal, complete the form, upload the required documents and pay the applicable fee before 11.59 pm on 28 November 2026. Second, keep the E-Samarth form number, and print the completed application with the payment receipt and supporting documents. Third, sign the printed set and superscribe the envelope with the post, pay level, department and E-Samarth form number. Fourth, send the set to the Registrar, Indian Institute of Information Technology Pune, PO Talegaon, Pune, Maharashtra 410507, so that it arrives by 5.30 pm on 9 December 2026.</p>
<p>For readers in Nepal, this is an Indian institute recruitment: apply only through the two official Samarth portals named above, pay only the fee stated in the notification, and treat any agent who promises a post, or asks for payment outside the official route, as fraud. No third-party page can file an IIIT Pune application on a candidate's behalf, and the institute's own notification, not a job-board summary, is the final word on eligibility and documents.</p>
<p>Growentix also covers <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ibps-server-administrator-assistant-programming-assistant-20261029">the IBPS direct recruitment for Server Administrator, Assistant and Programming Assistant posts</a> and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bel-probationary-engineer-350-posts-20261028">the Bharat Electronics Limited probationary engineer recruitment for 350 posts</a>. The IIIT Pune reporting here is drawn from <a href="https://www.edexlive.com/news/iiit-pune-recruitment-2026-25-teaching-non-teaching-posts">the Edex Live report on the IIIT Pune notification</a> and <a href="https://facultyvacancy.com/job/iiit-pune-faculty-recruitment-2026-17-assistant-professor-vacancies/">the FacultyVacancy listing for the 17 Assistant Professor posts</a>, which agree on the post counts, pay levels, dates and fees; candidates should verify the specialisations and eligibility conditions in the detailed advertisement on the official IIIT Pune website.</p>
